## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design scalable, multi-tenant data pipelines that handle schema diversity, guarantee data quality, and maintain operational reliability under high throughput.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant schema registry and validation
- Idempotent upserts using Iceberg MERGE operations
- Late data handling with time-partitioned snapshots
- Data quality enforcement via JSON Schema and Great Expectations
- Observability through comprehensive monitoring and automated rollback testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function upsertEvent(table, event) {
  // Validate against tenant-specific schema
  const isValid = validateEvent(event.tenant_id, event);
  if (!isValid) throw new Error('Schema validation failed');

  // Perform idempotent upsert using MERGE
  return table.merge()
    .whenMatched().updateAll()
    .whenNotMatched().insertAll()
    .execute();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-tenant data contracts, runtime validation, privacy masking, and governance in a real-time setting. Also probes trade-offs between Spark and Flink, plus testing strategies and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Runtime data contracts per tenant
- Per-tenant masking/redaction strategies
- GDPR deletion and data sovereignty
- Schema evolution in lakehouse (Iceberg/Parquet)
- Policy engine governance (e.g., OPA)
- Spark Structured Streaming vs Flink trade-offs
- Testing, monitoring, data quality

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo runtime contract check
function validateRecord(record, contract) {
  for (const field of Object.keys(contract.fields)) {
    if (!record.hasOwnProperty(field) && contract.fields[field].required) {
      throw new Error(`Missing required field ${field}`);
    }
  }
  // redaction example
  if (contract.mask) {
    for (const f of contract.mask) {
      if (record[f]) record[f] = "REDACTED";
    }
  }
  return record;
}
```

